  "lineage": "Developed in Lagos, Accra, Bamako and Dakar from the late 1950s through the 1970s in the dance-band highlife orbit — Fela Kuti's pre-Afrobeat Koola Lobitos, Guy Warren, Manu Dibango, the Bembeya and Rail Band circles — setting bebop and hard-bop horn language over highlife and Mande grooves: 4/4 or 12/8 clave-adjacent patterns, tenor and trumpet lead lines, clean single-coil guitar arpeggios, kora or balafon lines, and long vamp-based solo sections.",
